 <div class="note card" style="margin-top:12px;">
 CMS attributes the 2026 Part B premium jump mainly to projected price increases and higher utilization. CMS says the increase would have been larger if it hadn't acted to curb spending on "skin substitutes," a billing category flagged for fraud risk. This is a program-cost figure (what CMS spends and charges), not a CPI inflation rate.
 </div>
 <div class="source-card card" style="margin-top:12px;">
 <a href="https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/2026-medicare-parts-b-premiums-deductibles" target="_blank">CMS — 2026 Medicare Parts A &amp; B Premiums and Deductibles</a>
